":"8. How can I transition from a non-technical role to AI and data analytics?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You can start by learning Excel, SQL, Python, and basic statistics. Practice analyzing real datasets and building visualizations. Certifications and online courses help you gain credibility while you gradually move into analytics-focused roles.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/will-ai-replace-data-analysts\/#faq-question-1771415597770","position":9,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/will-ai-replace-data-analysts\/#faq-question-1771415597770","name":"9. Are certifications necessary for a career in data analytics?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Certifications are not always necessary, but they can help you learn structured skills, build credibility, and improve your chances of getting shortlisted for entry-level data analytics job opportunities.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/will-ai-replace-data-analysts\/#faq-question-1771415609470","position":10,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/will-ai-replace-data-analysts\/#faq-question-1771415609470","name":"10. What industries are hiring AI and data analytics professionals the most?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You\u2019ll find opportunities in finance, healthcare, IT, retail, e-commerce, and marketing. Any data-driven industry increasingly relies on analytics and AI, creating roles for professionals who can extract insights and improve business performance.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/will-ai-replace-data-analysts\/#faq-question-1771415620538","position":11,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/will-ai-replace-data-analysts\/#faq-question-1771415620538","name":"11. How long does it take to become proficient in data analytics?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You can become job-ready in 6\u201312 months by learning key tools, practicing real projects, and gaining hands-on experience. Full mastery takes longer, but consistent practice helps you confidently handle data and AI-related tasks.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/will-ai-replace-data-analysts\/#faq-question-1771415631621","position":12,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/will-ai-replace-data-analysts\/#faq-question-1771415631621","name":"12. What entry-level jobs are available in AI and data analytics?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You can start as a data analyst, junior data scientist, business analyst, or reporting analyst. These roles help you learn data manipulation, visualization, and AI basics while preparing you for higher-level positions.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"}]}},"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/17351","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/13"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=17351"}],"version-history":[{"count":7,"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/17351\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":22688,"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/17351\/revisions\/22688"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/17354"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=17